From: Halcyon Browser Project <halcyon@local>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] chrome_command_ids: Add Halcyon commands

Adds the command IDs that Halcyon's menu and keyboard shortcuts reference.
These are:
  - IDC_HALCYON_TOGGLE_TIDEMARKS
  - IDC_HALCYON_TOGGLE_QUIET_MODE
  - IDC_HALCYON_OPEN_LANTERN
  - IDC_HALCYON_OPEN_CAIRN
  - IDC_HALCYON_OPEN_TIDES
  - IDC_HALCYON_OPEN_COVE
  - IDC_HALCYON_ADD_MARGIN_NOTE
  - IDC_HALCYON_OPEN_QUILL

The IDs are added at the end of the ChromeCommand enum so they don't
conflict with any upstream IDs. The corresponding command handlers are
implemented in HalcyonBrowserCommandController (new file in
chrome/browser/ui/halcyon_browser_command_controller.cc).

---
 chrome/browser/ui/commands/chrome_command_ids.h | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/commands/chrome_command_ids.h b/chrome/browser/ui/commands/chrome_command_ids.h
index 0000000..1111111 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/commands/chrome_command_ids.h
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/commands/chrome_command_ids.h
@@ -450,4 +450,14 @@ enum ChromeCommand {
   ...
+  // Halcyon original features. (See brand_book.md §13.)
+  IDC_HALCYON_TOGGLE_TIDEMARKS,            // ⌘⇧L
+  IDC_HALCYON_TOGGLE_QUIET_MODE,            // ⌘⇧M
+  IDC_HALCYON_OPEN_LANTERN,                  // click the Lantern indicator
+  IDC_HALCYON_OPEN_CAIRN,                    // click the Cairn indicator
+  IDC_HALCYON_OPEN_TIDES,                    // ⌘Y
+  IDC_HALCYON_OPEN_COVE,                     // ⌘⇧N
+  IDC_HALCYON_ADD_MARGIN_NOTE,               // right-click → Add margin note
+  IDC_HALCYON_OPEN_QUILL,                     // ⌘⇧K
 };
